  "decision": "Approved",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<p>The development hereby approved shall only be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans and documents:</p><ul><li><span style=\"font-family: Arial, sans-serif; text-align: justify;\">Site Location Plan (02/01/2025)</span></li><li>Existing Floor Plans (drawing no.: 2025-002-005,\r\n     revision: A, dated: February 2025)</li><li>Existing Elevations (drawing no.: 2025-002-006,\r\n     revision: A, dated: February 2025)</li><li>Planning, Design and Access Statement (dated:\r\n     02/05/2025) Planning Note TVRS (received: 13/05/2025)</li><li>Environmental Noise Assessment (dated: 29/04/2025)</li><li>Transport Assessment (dated: April 2025)</li><li>Cover Letter (dated: 02/05/2025)&nbsp;</li></ul><p>No other drawings or documents apply.</p>",
    "1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\nOperational Management Plan&nbsp;\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nThe children’s home shall operate in accordance with the\r\nsubmitted Operational Management Plan, including the commitment to prioritise\r\nreferrals from the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham. The applicant shall\r\nnotify the Council of any forthcoming placements and provide confirmation of\r\nreferral origin upon request, unless otherwise agreed by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\nSecure by DesignPrior to the continued operation of the care home, details\r\ndemonstrating that the proposed development has achieved Secured by Design\r\ncertification shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local\r\nPlanning Authority in consultation with the Metropolitan Police All security\r\nmeasures applied to the approved development shall be permanently retained\r\nthereafter.",
    "1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\nCycle Parking(a)&nbsp; Prior to the continued operation of the\r\ncare home, details including the design and location\r\nof all cycle parking spaces shall be submitted to and approved in writing by\r\nthe Local Planning authority. All cycle storage should be designed and laid out\r\nin accordance with the guidance contained in the London Cycling Design\r\nStandards.\r\n\r\n(b)&nbsp; The approved\r\ndetails shall be implemented prior to first use of the development and\r\nthereafter permanently retained for the lifetime of the development.&nbsp;"
  ],
